Package: heterogeneity
Title: Explore Heterogeneous Effects with Causal Forests
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Saurabh", "Khanna", email = "saurabh.khanna2701@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Explores whether the effect of an independent variable on a
    dependent variable is larger for some people than for others. One call
    fits an honest causal forest via 'grf' and reports the average treatment
    effect (also in standard deviations for a continuous dependent variable),
    the spread of the estimated treatment effects and the characteristics the
    forest used most; a second function shows how the treatment effect varies
    with each candidate moderator, alone or with a second one, using grf's
    doubly robust scores for every average. The independent variable
    can have two values (differences) or be numeric (slopes). Missing
    characteristics use native forest handling without imputation. A 'shiny'
    app provides the same descriptive workflow for uploaded data or an
    included example from the 2024 General Social Survey.
